      { "text": "Sympathetic activation of brown adipose tissue lipolysis raises core temperature without requiring any change in hypothalamic set point.", "explanation": "Incorrect. BAT activation is a downstream EFFECTOR engaged after the set point has been raised by PGE2; the central change in fever is the elevated set point itself. This would be the correct answer if asking how a newborn responds to acute cold exposure, where no set-point change occurs." },
      { "text": "Direct viral invasion of the preoptic warmth-sensitive neurons mechanically disrupts their function and prevents heat dissipation.", "explanation": "Incorrect. Fever does not require direct CNS infection; the cytokine-PGE2 pathway operates equally well for bacterial sepsis from peripheral sites and for non-infectious tissue damage. This would be the correct answer if asking the mechanism of central fever in encephalitis with hypothalamic involvement." }
