    "questionText": "An ice fisherman becomes trapped on the open ice for several hours in -15 C wind. By the time he is brought to a warming shelter, his core temperature is 33.5 C. He is conscious but cannot articulate clearly; his arms and jaw shake in coarse, rhythmic, involuntary contractions that he cannot suppress, and his attempts to use a zipper or hold a cup are clumsy. He has no neurologic injury or alcohol on board. The faculty described an unusual reorganization of motor control under severe cold stress that produces this picture. Which mechanism best explains both his involuntary shaking and the impairment of his voluntary fine motor skills?",
